    {
      "id": "5f199f997089-q7",
      "number": 7,
      "question": "What is the simplified form of the following expression? \\({\\left( {x - \\frac{1}{y}} \\right)^3} + {\\left( {x + \\frac{1}{y}} \\right)^3}\\)",
      "questionHtml": "<p>What is the simplified form of the following expression?</p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\({\\left( {x - \\frac{1}{y}} \\right)^3} + {\\left( {x + \\frac{1}{y}} \\right)^3}\\)</span></p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "\\(x\\left( {{x^2} - \\frac{3}{{{y^2}}}} \\right)\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(x\\left( {{x^2} - \\frac{3}{{{y^2}}}} \\right)\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "\\( - 2x\\left( {{x^2} + \\frac{3}{{{y^2}}}} \\right)\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\( - 2x\\left( {{x^2} + \\frac{3}{{{y^2}}}} \\right)\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "\\(2x\\left( {{x^2} - \\frac{1}{{{y^2}}}} \\right)\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(2x\\left( {{x^2} - \\frac{1}{{{y^2}}}} \\right)\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "\\(2x\\left( {{x^2} + \\frac{3}{{{y^2}}}} \\right)\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(2x\\left( {{x^2} + \\frac{3}{{{y^2}}}} \\right)\\)</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<span style='display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;'><img height='26px' src='//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png' width='26px' /> <u style='font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; display: inline !important;'>Shortcut Trick</u></span>\n<p>Use Algebraic Identity: (a − b)<sup>3</sup> + (a + b)<sup>3</sup> = 2a(a<sup>2</sup> + 3b<sup>2</sup>).</p>\n<p>Here, a = x and b = 1/y.</p>\n<p>Substitute: 2(x)[(x)<sup>2</sup> + 3(1/y)<sup>2</sup>].</p>\n<p>Simplified result: 2x(x<sup>2</sup> + 3/y<sup>2</sup>).</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct answer is 2x(x<sup>2</sup> + 3/y<sup>2</sup>).</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style='display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;'><img height='26px' src='//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/alternate-methord-image.png' width='26px' /><strong><span style='vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;'><u>Alternate Method</u></span></strong></span></p>\n<p>Given: (x − 1/y)<sup>3</sup> + (x + 1/y)<sup>3</sup></p>\n<p>Formula used: (a − b)<sup>3</sup> = a<sup>3</sup> − 3a<sup>2</sup>b + 3ab<sup>2</sup> − b<sup>3</sup> and (a + b)<sup>3</sup> = a<sup>3</sup> + 3a<sup>2</sup>b + 3ab<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>3</sup></p>\n<p>⇒ Expansion of (x − 1/y)<sup>3</sup> = x<sup>3</sup> − 3x<sup>2</sup>/y + 3x/y<sup>2</sup> − 1/y<sup>3</sup></p>\n<p>⇒ Expansion of (x + 1/y)<sup>3</sup> = x<sup>3</sup> + 3x<sup>2</sup>/y + 3x/y<sup>2</sup> + 1/y<sup>3</sup></p>\n<p>⇒ Summing both expressions: (x<sup>3</sup> − 3x<sup>2</sup>/y + 3x/y<sup>2</sup> − 1/y<sup>3</sup>) + (x<sup>3</sup> + 3x<sup>2</sup>/y + 3x/y<sup>2</sup> + 1/y<sup>3</sup>)</p>\n<p>⇒ Combining like terms: (x<sup>3</sup> + x<sup>3</sup>) + (−3x<sup>2</sup>/y + 3x<sup>2</sup>/y) + (3x/y<sup>2</sup> + 3x/y<sup>2</sup>) + (−1/y<sup>3</sup> + 1/y<sup>3</sup>)</p>\n<p>⇒ Result = 2x<sup>3</sup> + 6x/y<sup>2</sup></p>\n<p>⇒ Taking 2x common: 2x(x<sup>2</sup> + 3/y<sup>2</sup>)</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct answer is 2x(x<sup>2</sup> + 3/y<sup>2</sup>).</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style='display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;'><img height='26px' src='//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png' width='26px' /><strong><span style='vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;'><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n<p style='margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;'>Cubic Identity (Difference)</p>\n<p style='margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;'>(a + b)<sup>3</sup> − (a − b)<sup>3</sup> = 2b(3a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>) = 6a<sup>2</sup>b + 2b<sup>3</sup></p>\n<p style='margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;'>Algebraic Square Identities</p>\n<p style='margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;'>(a + b)<sup>2</sup> + (a − b)<sup>2</sup> = 2(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>) and (a + b)<sup>2</sup> − (a − b)<sup>2</sup> = 4ab</p>\n<p style='margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;'>Sum and Difference of Cubes</p>\n<p style='margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;'>a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> = (a + b)(a<sup>2</sup> − ab + b<sup>2</sup>) and a<sup>3</sup> − b<sup>3</sup> = (a − b)(a<sup>2</sup> + ab + b<sup>2</sup>)</p>",
      "images": [
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png",
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/alternate-methord-image.png",
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png"
